// Date: 2024-04-25 | Modified: 2026-11-21
// ATT&CK: discovery, T1046
// Description: Detects usage of SoftPerfect's "netscan.exe". An application for scanning networks. It is
//   actively used in-the-wild by threat actors to inspect and understand the network architecture of
//   a victim.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate administrator activity
// References:
//   - https://www.protect.airbus.com/blog/uncovering-cyber-intruders-netscan/
//   - https://secjoes-reports.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/Sockbot%2Bin%2BGoLand.pdf
//   - https://www.sentinelone.com/labs/black-basta-ransomware-attacks-deploy-custom-edr-evasion-tools-tied-to-fin7-threat-actor/
//   - https://symantec-enterprise-blogs.security.com/blogs/threat-intelligence/yanluowang-ransomware-attacks-continue
//   - https://www.nccgroup.com/research/climbing-mount-everest-black-byte-bytes-back/
//   - https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/microsoft-exchange-servers-hacked-to-deploy-hive-ransomware/
//   - https://www.softperfect.com/products/networkscanner/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/9493cf5c565d7a01b8f064e01a51e1b94057e4bb/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_pua_netscan.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\netscan.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoProductName =~ "Network Scanner" or ProcessVersionInfoFileDescription =~ "Application for scanning networks"
